From 12c6d08056a82003f68085857181a60f430c20ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:10:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sim): march 256 steps and give an exact verdict at
 exhaustion

The stock preview march stopped after 64 steps. Over a flat face each
step is 0.9 x the height, so a ray at a few degrees ran out, got no
verdict, and the composite showed the grid through the cut stock.

Both twins (march.rs and trace.wgsl) now take 256 steps. A ray that
still runs out gets a hit only where material is proved on the ray
(the last sample, or the hit law's probe one cell on, is inside); a
bisection of that bracket puts the hit within 1/64 cell. Every other
exhausted ray keeps no verdict, so a near miss is never painted.

Pinned by a_grazing_faced_floor_resolves_and_stays_see_through.

Fixes #3612

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
